<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dwight D. Eisenhower</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Eisenhower</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dwight D. Eisenhower was a US general and President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> from 1953 to 1961. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-crisis">Suez Crisis</a> of 1956 he pressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to withdraw from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> by threatening to withhold financial support for the pound, a humiliation that exposed the limits of British power and accelerated the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower.jpg" alt="Dwight D. Eisenhower" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: White House · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dwight_D._Eisenhower,_official_photo_portrait,_May_29,_1959_(cropped)(3).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
